 "_regions": "First match wins. mountain = the Sierra Nevada above the foothills (Tahoe, Truckee, Grass Valley/Nevada City, Yosemite gateways, Mammoth, Kern River valley) plus hand-set mountain towns elsewhere (setSide: Big Bear, Lake Arrowhead, Idyllwild, Julian, Mount Shasta area); desert = the Mojave and Colorado deserts and the Owens Valley (Antelope Valley, Victor Valley, Coachella and Imperial valleys, Inyo); valley = the Central Valley from Redding to Bakersfield, with its foothill towns; north = the far north and the north coast (Humboldt, Del Norte, Mendocino, Lake County west of Clear Lake, Siskiyou, Modoc, Lassen); socal = the rest south of 34.5 (LA, Orange, San Diego, Ventura, Santa Barbara coast, Inland Empire); central = the Central Coast between 34.5 and 37.1 (Santa Cruz to Santa Maria); everything else is bay (the Bay Area, Napa/Sonoma, Clear Lake east shore).",
 "_exclude": "Vernon and Industry: industrial-only cities with almost no residents.",
 "_cdp": "California has 482 incorporated cities, so CDPs are kept only by hand (cdpMinPop is effectively off): keepCdp lists well-known mountain, north, desert, coast and Gold Country communities that fill the smaller climate pools, plus a few big, well-known unincorporated places. Suburban-tract CDPs are left out.",
 "_setSide": "Mountain towns outside the Sierra polygon: the San Bernardino, San Gabriel, San Jacinto and Cuyamaca mountains and Frazier Park (Mount Pinos). Maricopa (southwest Kern County) is a valley town just outside the polygon; Clearlake goes with the rest of Lake County (north).",
 "_rename": "Census names with the official long form in front: the cities are signed and known as Ventura and Paso Robles. The CDPs Sunnyside-Tahoe City and Idyllwild-Pine Cove are known as Tahoe City and Idyllwild.",
 "_keepCdp": "Names after rename (the tool renames first): Tahoe City and Idyllwild are the Census CDPs Sunnyside-Tahoe City and Idyllwild-Pine Cove."
}